CorvCAD patch series for KiCad 10.0.6 (caf7377), on top of 0001: let the schematic slice
compile against the wxWidgets iOS port (osx_iphone), which has no property grid, AUI, GL
canvas, status bar or info bar (wxUSE_PROPGRID/AUI/GLCANVAS/STATUSBAR/INFOBAR are 0).

Applied by integrations/kicad_core/fetch.py. The desktop probe still builds every unit and
matches kicad-cli; split per item before sending upstream.

1. Editor-only code moves out of model files: ERC/DRC tree model (RC_TREE_MODEL) from
   rc_item.cpp to the new common/rc_tree_model.cpp; STATUSBAR_REPORTER::Report() to
   widgets/kistatusbar.cpp; WarnUserIfOperatingSystemUnsupported() from common.cpp to
   confirm.cpp.
2. The property system uses a small wxPGChoices stand-in (properties/pg_choices_fallback.h,
   same semantics) when wxWidgets has no property grid.
3. AUI pane state in settings (aui_settings.cpp, JSON_SETTINGS, EESCHEMA_SETTINGS defaults) is
   compiled only when wxUSE_AUI.
4. iOS (__WXOSX_IPHONE__): PGM_BASE skips the tooltip setup and the preferred-editor file
   dialog, which wx iOS declares but does not implement; the "all files" wildcard is "*".
5. Headers stop pulling in editor widgets: gl_context_mgr.h forward-declares wxGLCanvas and
   wxGLContext, sch_field.h forward-declares SCINTILLA_TRICKS and wxStyledTextEvent (users
   include scintilla_tricks.h), ibis_parser.h drops wx_html_report_panel.h, git_progress.h
   reports through PROGRESS_REPORTER, and sch_text/sch_textbox drop sch_navigate_tool.h.
